  "description": "It was discovered that RenderDoc did not properly verify array sizes when\nserialising strings, leading to an integer overflow. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a buffer overflow, resulting in a denial\nof service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2023-33863)\n\nIt was discovered that RenderDoc incorrectly handled certain socket reads,\nleading to an integer overflow. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause a heap buffer overflow, resulting in a denial of service, or\npossibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2023-33864)\n\nIt was discovered that RenderDoc followed symbolic links when opening its\nlog file in the /tmp/RenderDoc directory. A local attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to escalate privileges. (CVE-2023-33865)",
  "id": "USN-9124-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in RenderDoc.",
